# Dual-Repo Sync Rule

The **Profitability** repo (`c:\Users\RoryIgo\repos\cursor\Profitability`) is the
deployed source of truth. The **sage-framework** repo
(`c:\Users\RoryIgo\repos\sage-framework`) is the framework specification mirror.

## Mirrored file mappings

| sage-framework path | Profitability path |
|---|---|
| `AGENTS.md` | `AGENTS.md` |
| `agents/*.md` | `agents/*.md` |
| `rules/*.mdc` | `rules/*.mdc` |
| `skills/**` | `skills/**` |
| `templates/*` | `templates/*` |
| `.mcp.json` | `.mcp.json` |
| `hooks-spec/hooks.json` | `hooks/hooks.json` |
| `hooks-spec/scripts/*.py` | `hooks/scripts/*.py` |
| `hooks-spec/workflow-config.json` | `.sage/workflow-config.json` |

## Required behaviour

When you modify any file listed in the mapping table above:

1. **Apply the same change to both repos.** Do not modify one copy without
   updating the other.
2. **State which files in each repo were updated** in your response so the
   user can verify sync.
3. If you are unsure whether a file is mirrored, check the mapping table.
   Files not listed (e.g. `agent-definitions.md`, `cursor-directory-spec/`,
   `docs/`, `reference-docs/`) exist only in sage-framework and do not
   require a Profitability counterpart.

## Spec documents

When a mirrored file changes, check whether any sage-framework spec document
references the changed content and update the spec if needed:

- `cursor-directory-spec/cursor-directory-spec.md`
- `hooks-spec/hook-scripts-spec.md`
- `hooks-spec/session-manifest-schema.md`
